description:
LAND THIS BEFORE THE SOURCE PORT (execution step 4, ahead of step 5) so
it guards the work rather than auditing it afterwards.

Rewrite packages/solid-form/eslint.config.js — currently 5 lines that just re-export the
root config:

  // @ts-check

  import rootConfig from '../../eslint.config.js'

  export default [
    ...rootConfig,
    {
      files: ['src/**'],
      rules: {
        // Solid 2 treats the effect half's return value as a cleanup slot: any
        // non-undefined, non-function value throws in dev and permanently halts
        // the reactive system (REACTIVITY_HALTED), silently, process-wide. An
        // expression-bodied arrow leaks its expression's value into that slot,
        // so effect halves must be braced blocks.
        'no-restricted-syntax': [
          'error',
          {
            selector:
              "CallExpression[callee.name=/^create(Render)?Effect$/][arguments.1.type='ArrowFunctionExpression'][arguments.1.body.type!='BlockStatement']",
            message:
              'Effect halves must be braced blocks returning undefined or a cleanup function: an expression-bodied arrow leaks its value into the cleanup slot and halts reactivity (REACTIVITY_HALTED).',
          },
        ],
      },
    },
  ]

Transcription notes: drop table's intermediate empty { rules: {} } object — it is dead
weight. Use the plain-array form, not store's defineConfig() wrapper, because this repo's
root eslint.config.js exports a plain array. Scope to src/** only: the tests legitimately
use single-argument createEffect (createFormHook.test.tsx:592), which the selector does
not match anyway since it keys on arguments.1, but scoping keeps the intent clear.

If the source port later introduces createTrackedEffect or an onSettled with an
expression body, extend the regex.

The root @tanstack/eslint-config has no Solid-specific rules and does not set
no-restricted-syntax, so this entry clobbers nothing.

packages/solid-form/src/createFieldGroup.tsx, 239 lines. Two changes,
one of which is a real bug fix with an API break.

(1) Mount, :209-217. DROP the mounted flag entirely — it is written at :212 and :215 and
read nowhere, dead in Solid 1 too. FieldGroupApi.mount() is () => () => {}, so there is
nothing to preserve:

  // onSettled registers the callback's return value as cleanup, replacing the Solid 1
  // onMount + nested onCleanup pair (onCleanup throws inside onSettled).
  onSettled(() => api.mount())

(2) Subscribe, :203-207. This is finding M5: a PRE-EXISTING staleness bug that Solid 2
only reveals. functionalUpdate(props.children, data()) evaluates data() in a component
body, and createComponent runs component bodies inside untrack() — in Solid 1 as well —
so a child like {(lastName) => <p>{lastName}</p>} inserts a plain string once and never
updates. The existing tests at createFormHook.test.tsx:274 and :327 pass only because
the value never changes in them.

  extendedApi.Subscribe = (props) => {
    const data = useSelector(api.store, props.selector)

    // Pass the accessor, not data(). A component body is untracked, so an eager read
    // here hands the child a value frozen at first render — the shape Solid 2's
    // [STRICT_READ_UNTRACKED] diagnostic exists to catch.
    return functionalUpdate(props.children, data)
  }

and the type at :68-71:

    Subscribe: <TSelected = NoInfer<FieldGroupState<TFieldGroupData>>>(props: {
      selector?: (state: NoInfer<FieldGroupState<TFieldGroupData>>) => TSelected
      children:
        | ((state: Accessor<NoInfer<TSelected>>) => JSX.Element)
        | JSX.Element
    }) => JSX.Element

The `as Element` cast at :206 goes away — it was casting to the DOM lib's global Element,
unrelated to Solid's element type, and only compiled because functionalUpdate's output
type is free.

Plus imports: drop onMount, add onSettled; JSX type from @solidjs/web (:4); JSX.Element
already in use at :70-71.

This makes createFieldGroup.Subscribe consistent with createForm.Subscribe, which
already passes the accessor. It is a typed, visible API break and needs a changeset
entry (see the release epic).

packages/solid-form/src/createFormGroup.tsx, 622 lines. Structurally
identical to createField.tsx — do that one first and mirror it. Three changes, same as
2.4 but with one selector instead of seven.

(1) makeFormGroupReactive, :115-125:

  // Identity selector: @tanstack/store hands out a new snapshot object per write,
  // so === on the snapshot already deduplicates.
  const store = useSelector(formGroupApi.store, (s) => s)

  return createMemo(
    () => {
      store()
      return formGroupApi
    },
    { equals: false, name: 'form/formGroup' },
  )

The existing comment at :116 ("Handle shallow comparison to make sure that Derived
doesn't create a new setGroup call every time") describes the old signal mechanism and
should be replaced by the accurate one above.

(2) Mount + options loop, :198-218 — identical shape to createField:

  let mounted = false
  onSettled(() => {
    const cleanupFn = api.mount()
    mounted = true
    return () => {
      cleanupFn()
      mounted = false
    }
  })

  createRenderEffect(
    () => trackOptions(opts()),
    (nextOptions) => {
      if (!mounted) return
      untrack(() => api.update(nextOptions))
    },
  )

FormGroupApi.mount() returns a real cleanup (it writes formGroupStateBase and registers
the instance), so the returned-cleanup form is load-bearing here, not just idiomatic.

(3) Seeding read, :194: const options = untrack(opts)

Plus imports (drop createComputed/createSignal/onMount; add createMemo,
createRenderEffect, onSettled, untrack, trackOptions), JSX from @solidjs/web, and
JSXElement -> JSX.Element at :427 and :521.

Note the source comment at :213 says "createComputed to make sure this effect runs
before render effects" — that intent is preserved by createRenderEffect, whose effect
half runs in the render queue ahead of ordinary effects and ahead of onSettled. Update
the comment to say so rather than deleting it.
